   "en": "SH43 is a journey into the folds of the country rather than a fast link between towns. Plan it in daylight, with a fuelled vehicle and no tight appointment in Stratford. Its former gravel gap through the Tāngarākau Gorge was sealed in 2024–25, but the road still has narrow sections, bends and the Moki Tunnel. The satisfying version of the day is simple: gorge, tunnel, a long stop at Whangamōmona, then the saddles toward Taranaki. Add an overnight if you want the rail-cart experience as well.",
